[.items] 

category_short_name: public_transportation 

text: Public transportation funding tends to go to places with lower transportation costs and greater access to employment.

 

category_short_name: roads_and_bridges 

text: Funding for roads and bridges tends to go to places that are heavily reliant on car travel already.

 

category_short_name: broadband 

text: Broadband programs direct more funding to places with less internet access and lower broadband speeds.

 

category_short_name: housing_and_community_development 

text: Housing and community development funds are distributed more often to places with higher housing cost burdens and more overcrowding.

 

category_short_name: passenger_and_freight_rail 

text: Passenger and freight rail funds are disproportionately distributed to places without intercity passenger rail service.

 

category_short_name: ports 

text: Airport and dock programs tend to fund areas with existing airports and docks, rather than investing in new areas.

 

category_short_name: energy_and_power 

text: Energy and power programs direct similar levels of funding to places with high household energy costs as to places with lower household energy costs.

 

category_short_name: environmental_resilience 

text: Environmental resilience programs direct more funding to places with low incomes.

 

category_short_name: water_conservation 

text: Water conservation programs send more funds to places with more water system violations.

