state_about_text: This page details funding through major infrastructure programs distributed to [state] in fiscal years 2022 through 2025, with many of those funds distributed directly to local governments and private entities and not used by the state government.

 

county_about_text: This page details funding through major infrastructure programs distributed to [county] in fiscal years 2022 through 2025. Some funds were distributed directly to local governments, public agencies, and private entities within the county, and were not used by the county government. In some cases, a funding obligation for a statewide effort may list the state government as the recipient and the state capital as the recipient location. While we have taken steps to account for this, there may still be cases in this tool where counties that contain state capitals appear to receive more money than they actually received.

 

cbsa_about_text: This page details funding through major infrastructure programs distributed to [CBSA] in fiscal years 2022 through 2025. Core-based statistical areas (CBSAs) include metropolitan and micropolitan areas, which are made up of an urban area and its surrounding communities. This page includes funds for entities or projects located within the boundaries of the CBSA. In some cases, a funding obligation for a statewide effort may list the state government as the recipient and the state capital as the recipient location. While we have taken steps to account for this, there may still be cases in this tool where CBSAs that contain state capitals appear to receive more money than they actually received.

 

